    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0391" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg297"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 379.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 27th instant, referring to previous correspondence
                    relative to the United States regulations for the transportation of cattle to
                    Europe and inclosing copies of dispatches on the subject received by you from
                    Her Majesty’s consul-general at New York.</p>
                <p>The Department hopes to receive from you at an early day the promised report of
                    the British Board of Trade on the subject in order that the matter may be
                    finally disposed of.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
